<title>UK: Gasoline tanker touches bottom in France - Lloyds.</title>
<headline>Gasoline tanker touches bottom in France - Lloyds.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>An oil tanker carrying gasoline from Rouen, France to the United States touched bottom in the River Seine on Monday, Lloyds Shipping Intelligence Service reported.</p>
<p>The 1986-built Kriti Palm tanker, believed to be carrying 35,000 tonnes of gasoline, sailed to Le Havre for bottom inspection on Tuesday, Lloyds said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8145</p>
